From: conda-forge maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Use CppInterOp 2.0 typed public reflection API and native Clang session.

Jank owns its compiler and obtains LLJIT through LLVM's public builder
callback. Session-dependent operations use public Clang AST/Sema APIs;
stateless reflection uses the packaged CppInterOp API. No private
CppInterOp headers or interpreter layout are required.

